1
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,000
To save the world, they'll have to stick together.

2
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
The Day the Earth Blew Up: A Looney Tunes Movie is a family,
comedy, adventure film directed by Peter Browngardt.

3
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Porky and Daffy, the classic animated odd couple, turn into unlikely heroes when their
antics at the local bubble gum factory uncover a secret alien mind control plot.

4
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Against all odds, the two are determined to save their town (and the
world!)...that is if they don't drive each other crazy in the process.

5
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Porky Pig / Daffy Duck (voice), played by Eric Bauza.

6
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Petunia Pig / Old Lady (voice), played by Candi Milo.

7
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:36,000
The Invader (voice), played by Peter MacNicol.

8
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Scientist / Farmer Jim (voice), played by Fred Tatasciore.

9
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Mrs. Grecht (voice), played by Laraine Newman.

10
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Mayor (voice), played by Wayne Knight.

11
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
The Day the Earth Blew Up: A Looney Tunes Movie is a 2024 American
animated science fiction comedy film produced by Warner Bros.

12
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Directed by Pete Browngardt in his feature directorial debut, the film is a spin-off from the Looney Tunes Cartoons series developed by Browngardt,
and is the first fully animated and theatrically released film in the Looney Tunes franchise consisting of entirely original material.

13
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
It features the voices of Eric Bauza, Candi Milo, and Peter MacNicol.

14
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
The film follows Daffy Duck and Porky Pig as they try to save
Earth from a chewing gum-based alien scheme.

15
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
In 2019, while working on Looney Tunes Cartoons, Browngardt was asked if
he had any ideas for a new Looney Tunes feature film.

16
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Browngardt eventually settled on the premise of a "sci-fi
B-movie from the '50s" starring Daffy and Porky.

17
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
He took inspiration from features of the era and
shorts starring the cartoon duo.

18
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Warner Bros.

19
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Animation, alongside several vendors, provided the animation for the film, of which its
character designs were modeled after the style of animator Bob Clampett.

20
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Joshua Moshier, who previously worked on Looney Tunes
Cartoons, composed the film's score.

21
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Upon its announcement in 2021, The Day the Earth Blew Up was originally set to be
released on HBO Max and the "ACME Night" block on Cartoon Network.

22
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
Instead, however, the film premiered at the Annecy International Animation Film Festival on June 11, 2024, and had a limited
release in the United States on December 13, 2024, by Ketchup Entertainment, before expanding wide on March 14, 2025.

23
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and
grossed $15.3 million worldwide on a $15 million budget.

24
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film explores themes of chewing gum, zombie, alien
invasion, buddy comedy, duringcreditsstinger.

25
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
